  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="4346f584-c163-4d4f-af5b-ff3f4e32e6dc"><problem><para>
      <para>For questions 1 – 3, match each sequence with one of the definitions. Note that only the part of the definition showing the relationship between the current term and the previous term is given so as not to give away the solutions.</para>
      <para>6, 12, 18, 24</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(a(n)=7\cdot a(n-1)\)</para><para>\(b(n)=\frac12b(n-1)\)</para><para>\(c(n)=c(n-1)+6\)</para><para>\(d(n)=d(n-1)+20\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(c(n)=c(n-1)+6\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(c(n)=c(n−1)+6\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
